The graph shows a curve $y = f(x)$ with a tangent line drawn at $(2, 5)$ passing through $(0, 1)$ and $(4, 9)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:4.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.15*\x*\x + 0.4*\x + 1.1}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,0.5) -- (4.5,5.0);
\fill (2,2.5) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(2,5)$};
\fill (0,0.5) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(0,1)$};
\fill (4,4.5) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(4,9)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the estimated instantaneous rate of change $f'(2)$?

Water drains from a tank.
The volume $V$ (litres) after $t$ minutes is plotted, and the tangent line at $t = 4\text{ min}$ passes through $(0, 60)$ and $(8, 12)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$V$};
\foreach \x/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\val$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/20,2/40,3/60,4/80,5/100} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:5.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.6 + 3.262*exp(-0.5*\x)}) node[above right] {$V(t)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,3.0) -- (4,0.6);
\fill (2,1.8) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$(4,36)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Volume (L)};
\node[below] at (2.7,-0.9) {Time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the estimated instantaneous rate of change of the volume at $t = 4\text{ minutes}$?

The graph shows a curve $y = f(x)$ with a tangent line at $(2, 3)$ passing through $(0, -5)$ and $(3, 7)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (5.0,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {-2/-4,1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.3*\x*\x + 0.8*\x - 1.3}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.5,-1.5) -- (3.5,4.5);
\fill (2,1.5) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(2,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the estimated derivative $f'(2)$.
